  "texto": "# Arriving at the forest\n@energy 2\n> Slow and kind, like opening a door.\n\n[slow][soft]Close your eyes and let your breathing find its own pace.\nImagine you're at the edge of a southern forest, in Patagonia.\n[breathe]\nThe air is fresh and smells of damp earth and wood.\nThe trees are tall, with ancient trunks covered in moss.\nCan you hear the leaves crunch beneath your steps? [up]\n[breathe]\nWalk slowly, with no hurry at all.\nEach step takes you further from the noise of the city.\nYou're here now, and that's enough.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The trail\n@energy 1\n> Very soft; leave space between each image.\n\n[soft]The trail winds between ferns, plants and roots.\nLight comes through the branches in thin rays.\n[breathe]\nA small bird sings far away, and another one answers.\nFeel the soft ground under your feet, firm and steady.\nWith every step, your shoulders feel a little lighter.\n[breathe]\nIf a thought appears, let it go like a leaf in the wind.\nYou don't have to follow it.\nJust walk, breathe and look around.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The lake\n@energy 1\n> Almost a whisper, with deep calm.\n\n[slow][soft]All at once, the forest opens and a lake of clear water appears.\nIt's so still that it mirrors the mountains like glass.\n[breathe]\nYou sit on a warm stone by the shore.\nLook at the water: it doesn't move, it isn't in a hurry.\nYour mind can be like that too.\n[breathe]\nBreathe with the lake: slow on the way in, slower on the way out.\nListen to the silence, which here is vast and soft.\nStay for a moment without doing anything.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The snow\n@energy 2\n> Soft, with a touch of wonder.\n\n[soft]High above, on the peaks, the **snow** shines in the afternoon sun.\nImagine that clean white entering your chest with every breath.\n[breathe]\nAs you exhale, let tiredness leave, like a gray cloud drifting away.\nBreathe in white, breathe out gray, again and again.\nYour body feels lighter with each round.\n[breathe]\nDo you notice how much space there is inside you now? [up]\nThat space is yours too.\nYou can come back to it whenever you want.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Returning\n@energy 2\n> Come back with care; a warm tone at the end.\n\n[slow]Say goodbye to the lake with one last look.\nWalk back along the trail, unhurried, between the trees.[/slow]\n[breathe]\nLittle by little, the forest stays behind and you return to your room.\nFeel the weight of your body and the air around you.\n[breathe]\nMove your hands, stretch your back and open your eyes when you're ready.\nTake the forest's silence with you.\nIt's kept inside you, a quiet treasure for whenever you need it. [down]\nThank you for this walk.\n[pause 3s]\n"
