  "texto": "# Putting the phone down\n@energy 2\n> Kind and unhurried, without judging.\n\n[slow][soft]Before we begin, put your phone face down, out of reach.\nIf it buzzes, let it buzz: for a few minutes, nothing is urgent.\n[breathe]\nFind a comfortable position and rest your back.\nClose your eyes and notice your empty hands.\nDo you still feel the urge to check the screen? [up]\n[breathe]\nThat's okay; it's normal.\nJust watch the urge, like a car passing by the window.\nAnd let it drift away.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Your eyes\n@energy 1\n> Very soft, taking care with each word.\n\n[soft]Your eyes spend so many hours looking at bright lights.\nNow let them rest behind your eyelids.\n[breathe]\nFeel the small muscles around your eyes relax.\nYour forehead softens, and so do your eyebrows and your jaw.\n[breathe]\nImagine a warm, kind darkness, like a summer night.\nThere are no notifications or messages, only silence.\nYour mind can turn down the volume, like a screen at sunset.\nBreathe in, breathe out, and let everything dim a little.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Your body\n@energy 1\n> Almost a whisper, moving through the body with calm.\n\n[slow][soft]Now move your attention through your body, from head to toe.\nNotice your neck, which so often leans toward the screen.\nLet it return to its place, long and free.\n[breathe]\nMove down through your shoulders, your arms and your hands.\nFeel your fingers at rest, not typing, not scrolling.\n[breathe]\nContinue through your chest, your belly and your legs.\nYour whole body rests, with nothing to answer.\nThis is also a kind of **connection**: with yourself.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# What matters\n@energy 2\n> Soft, with a touch of reflection.\n\n[soft]Think of something you saw today without a screen in between.\nA face, a street, a square, or a painting on a wall.\n[breathe]\nWhat did you feel in that moment? [up]\nMaybe it was small, but it was real, and it was yours.\n[breathe]\nThe world outside is still there, waiting for you without hurry.\nThe news can wait a few more minutes.\nYour breath, on the other hand, is here now.\nStay with it a little longer.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Returning\n@energy 2\n> Come back with calm; a warm tone at the end.\n\n[slow]Begin to gently move your fingers and toes.\nStretch your arms and notice the air in the room.[/slow]\n[breathe]\nBefore you pick up your phone, take one more deep breath.\nDecide calmly what to check first, and what can wait.\nHere's a kind rule: breathe first, scroll later.\nIt's a small decision that changes your day.\n[breathe]\nOpen your eyes when you're ready.\nYou can give yourself this pause every day, even for five minutes.\nYour attention is valuable: take care of it. [down]\nThank you for giving yourself this time.\n[pause 3s]\n"
