  "texto": "# Arriving\n@energy 2\n> Calm and close, like someone keeping you company.\n\n[slow][soft]Tomorrow is an important day, and it's fine to feel it in your body.\nFind a comfortable position and close your eyes.\n[breathe]\nBreathe in through your nose and fill your chest little by little.\nExhale slowly, as if blowing out a candle with no hurry.\n[breathe]\nWhere do you feel the nerves right now? [up]\nMaybe in your stomach, your hands or your throat.\nYou don't have to make them disappear.\nWe're just going to give them some room.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Box breathing\n@energy 1\n> Very calm; count without rushing.\n\n[slow][soft]Let's breathe in four equal counts.\nBreathe in, counting to four: one, two, three, four.\nHold your breath, also for four counts.\nBreathe out for four, and wait four before starting again.\n[breathe]\nIt's like drawing a square with your breath, no hard rules.\nRepeat it a couple of times, at your own pace.\n[breathe]\nNotice how your heart begins to slow down.\nYour body knows how to calm itself; it just needs a reminder.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Imagining it goes well\n@energy 2\n> Soft, with a calm smile.\n\n[soft]Now picture tomorrow, but going well.\nYou see yourself arriving on time, with a steady step and your head up.\n[breathe]\nYou say hello, speak calmly and someone smiles back.\nIf something doesn't go as planned, you breathe and keep going.\n[breathe]\nYou don't need to know everything to begin.\nYou carry everything you've learned until today.\nAnd that's more than you think.\nHold that vision for a moment.\nKeep it like a **gift** for tomorrow.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Letting go\n@energy 1\n> Almost a whisper.\n\n[slow][soft]Now let go of the image and come back to the present.\nNotice the weight of your body, supported and safe.\n[breathe]\nWhatever needs to happen tomorrow will happen tomorrow.\nTonight, your only job is to rest.\nCan you leave tomorrow for tomorrow? [up]\nSoften your forehead, your shoulders and your hands.\n[breathe]\nFeel your breathing become slow and deep on its own.\nThere's no need to rush.\nEach exhale takes you a little closer to rest.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Returning or sleeping\n@energy 2\n> Very warm at the end.\n\n[slow]If you're going to sleep, stay like this and let sleep come by itself.\nIf you're going on with your evening, come back little by little.[/slow]\n[breathe]\nMove your fingers, stretch your arms and open your eyes with calm.\nRemember box breathing: it goes with you wherever you go.\n[breathe]\nTomorrow, before you walk in, take four breaths like this.\nYour nerves aren't an enemy; they're a sign that you care.\nTrust yourself. [down]\nSleep well, and good luck.\n[pause 3s]\n"
